  "col_left L16: «πρόσωπον» is Greek, with the acute on the first ο.",
  "col_left L17: the hyphen of «for-» is printed short, like a point at mid height (1.8 by 1.1 points).",
  "col_left L21, L32: the commas after «II» are printed short (1.6 by 2.5 and 1.6 by 2.4 points, their feet 0.7 point below the baseline).",
  "col_left L23: «Baṭlamyūs» has the dot under the t and the bar over the u.",
  "col_left L24: the lower left foot of the second X of «{sc:xxxv}» stands apart (1.9 by 1.4 points, on the baseline), like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_left L26: the lower arm of the L of «{sc:xlv}» stands apart from its stem (1.9 by 2.0 points, low on the line), and the left foot of the A of «Alba-» stands apart like a point; neither is a point.",
  "col_left L35: «Naṣīr ad-dīn» has the dot under the s and bars over both i.",
  "col_left L36: the hyphen of «284-287» is printed as a small point at mid height (1.2 by 1.2 points); read as a hyphen.",
  "col_left L39, L40, L41: «al-Ḥaǵǵāǵ» (three times) has the dot under the H, the acute on each g and the bar over the a; in L39 the bar touches the ear of the g before it. In L40 a speck (1.1 by 1.2 points) at mid height between the H and the a is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L39: «233 n ,» is printed without a point after the n: the comma stands 3.8 points after the n, where «n.,» has its point (after 113 in L30 of the right column the n, the point and the comma take 3.6 points); transcribed as printed.",
